4. Mandatory prominent attribution

Every permitted shared copy, adaptation, demonstration, publication, screenshot
or video containing a substantial part of the Material must clearly identify
its origin, using the following credit or an accurate translation:

  Based on Vancouver Living Atlas by YiTaChen
  Source: https://github.com/YiTaChen/vancouver-living-atlas
  License: Vancouver Living Atlas Noncommercial Research and Attribution 1.0

Include a link to the source and to its LICENSE where the medium supports links.
For modified versions, clearly state that the version is modified and identify
your changes; do not suggest it is an official release or endorsed by YiTaChen.

For source repositories and downloadable packages, place the credit prominently
near the beginning of the README or accompanying documentation, and include
this full LICENSE and all copyright notices. For websites or interactive demos,
show the project credit and source link in a legible, visible part of the main
interface, such as a footer; a hidden comment or a buried settings page is not
sufficient. For videos, include a readable credit in the video and in its
accompanying description; for images, use a visible credit or immediately
adjacent caption. For academic papers and presentations, include a proper
citation with the repository URL and, when available, the version/commit used.
These requirements apply to personal and privately shared presentations too.

